            <div class="container page-space-top pb-50" role="article">
                <div class="row">
                    <div class="col-xl-10 offset-xl-1">
                        <div class="p20 underline active">
                            <h1 class="h2">Serbia – Amendments on the rulebook of EMC and LVD</h1>
                        </div>

                                                                                                            <div class="date mb-30 text-bold">
                                <time datetime="2020-05-18">05/18/2020</time>
                            </div>
                        
                        <div class="mb-60 subtitle">EMC and LVD Certificates of Conformity (CoCs) will no longer be mandatory from January 1, 2022.</div>

                        <div class="pb-50">
                            <img width="340" height="170" src="https://cetecomadvanced.com/files/images/news/serbien-1.jpg" class="attachment-news-postintro size-news-postintro wp-post-image" alt="serbia" loading="eager" decoding="async" fetchpriority="high" srcset="https://cetecomadvanced.com/files/images/news/serbien-1.jpg 340w" sizes="(min-width: 1200px) 1253px, (max-width: 1199.98px) 886px, (max-width: 991.98px) 861px, (max-width: 767.98px) 637px, (max-width: 575.98px) 545px" />                        </div>

                                                    <p>Market approval for devices using radio technologies in Serbia are regulated by the Serbian authorities. While the requirements mainly base on the <a href="https://cetecomadvanced.com/en/news/red/">Radio Equipment Directive</a>, there are still some national requirements defined in the Serbian Official Gazette.</p>
<p>Recently, Regulation No. 21/2020 was published, which is an amendment to the rulebook on Electromagnetic Compatibility (EMC) and rulebook on the Electrical Equipment intended for use within Certain Voltage Limits (LVD).</p>
<p>The main change in the amendment is that Serbian <strong>EMC</strong> and <strong>LVD</strong> Certificates of Conformity (CoCs) will no longer be mandatory from <strong>1st January 2022</strong>. Instead, <a href="https://cetecomadvanced.com/en/certification/ce-marking/">CE marking</a> will be acceptable for non-radio devices to demonstrate compliance. Until this date, manufacturers should continue to seek <strong>EMC</strong> and <strong>LVD</strong> CoC&#8217;s for applicable equipment.</p>
<p>We have prepared further information on the <a href="https://cetecomadvanced.com/en/country-approval/serbia/">market approval for Serbia on the corresponding subpage for you.</a></p>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
<p><b>If you have any questions, please do not hesitate to contact us directly:</b></p>
<p><a href="https://cetecomadvanced.com/en/contact/">https://cetecomadvanced.com/en/contact/</a></p>
                        
                                            </div>
                </div>
            </div>

        
    </div>
